<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>FBS recovery and coverage · Sports Edge Lab</title><meta name="description" content="A partial model run, preserved numerical evidence, a reproducible checkpoint example and honest FBS source coverage."><link rel="stylesheet" href="dashboard.css"><style>
.recovery-page .panel{padding:24px}.certificate-grid>*{min-width:0}.case-status{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.recovery-hero{padding-bottom:44px}.recovery-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4.2rem)}.recovery-hero .badge{background:#8b4826;color:#fff}.run-strip{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}.run-step{padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--line,#c9d8df);border-radius:12px;background:white}.run-step strong{display:block;font-size:1.8rem}.certificate-controls{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0}.certificate-controls button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#006c67;color:white;outline:2px solid #006c67;outline-offset:2px}.certificate-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px}.certificate-grid dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;margin:0}.certificate-grid dt{color:#526775}.certificate-grid dd{margin:0;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.case-status{font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:750;color:#9b4427}.case-status.certified{color:#006c67}.coverage-bar{display:flex;width:100%;height:26px;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;margin:16px 0}.coverage-bar .mapped{background:#007e77;width:87.3015873016%}.coverage-bar .gap{background:#b96131;flex:1}.legend{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}.mono{font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.85rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.scope-note{font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6}.week-controls{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:16px 0}.week-controls select{width:auto;min-width:160px;padding:8px;border:1px solid #9dafb9;border-radius:6px;background:white;font:inherit}@media(max-width:700px){.recovery-page .panel{padding:16px}.run-strip,.certificate-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.certificate-grid dl{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr)}}
</style></head><body class="recovery-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to evidence</a><div class="topbar"><div class="shell"><a class="brand" href="index.html">SPORTS EDGE LAB <span>/ FBS</span></a><nav aria-label="Review navigation"><a href="index.html">Current season</a><a href="research.html">Historical study</a><a href="#recovery">Recovery demo</a><a href="#season">2026 replay</a><a href="#coverage">Coverage</a><a href="../../tracks/ncaaf/MODEL_CARD.md">Model card</a></nav></div></div>
<div class="shell" style="padding:18px 24px"><strong>Preserved V025 snapshot.</strong> V026 subsequently completed 100 new fits and recovered 197 verified states. <a href="index.html">Open the current season and market explorer →</a></div><header class="hero recovery-hero"><div class="shell hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Owner evidence / 03 NOV 2026 <span class="badge">V025 · PARTIAL</span></div><h1>Keep the work.<br><span>Prove the recovery.</span></h1><p>The next owner study stopped after one numerical optimizer failure. Its committed work survives. A complete new comparison still requires the unfinished stages.</p><div class="links"><a class="button primary" href="#recovery">Inspect the recovery example ↓</a><a class="button ghost" href="research.html">Completed study at this snapshot ↗</a></div></div><aside class="verdict"><div class="eyebrow">Actual owner accounting</div><h2>197 committed fits.<br>One failed attempt.</h2><p>198 forward fits were attempted. The 99 final learned states were not attempted. No new complete performance result, live issue, order or promotion is claimed.</p><p><strong>At this V025 snapshot, V024 was the last completed owner study.</strong> Its negative winner result stays visible.</p></aside></div></header>
<main id="main" class="shell"><section class="section" aria-labelledby="run-title"><div class="section-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Know which state you are reviewing</div><h2 id="run-title">Delivery succeeded. Research remains partial.</h2><p>A preserved diagnostic archive is useful evidence of a failure. It does not turn an incomplete experiment into a completed negative scientific result.</p></div></div><div class="run-strip"><article class="run-step"><div class="eyebrow">Completed</div><strong>197</strong><p>Committed learned states retained. Reuse requires exact input, code, environment and numerical verification.</p></article><article class="run-step"><div class="eyebrow">Failed</div><strong>1</strong><p>A numerical optimizer stopped. Its status is preserved; an uncertified iterate does not count as an accepted fit.</p></article><article class="run-step"><div class="eyebrow">Not attempted</div><strong>99</strong><p>Final states remain unfinished. Local tests and the public demonstration below count as zero owner fits.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="recovery" class="section" aria-labelledby="recovery-title"><div class="section-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / Reproduce a mechanism</div><h2 id="recovery-title">A solver flag is one piece of evidence.</h2><p>These invented convex problems reuse the repository’s existing exact rational certificate. No private objective, feature formula, weight or sports prediction is exposed.</p></div><span class="tag">Invented fixtures only</span></div><div class="panel"><div class="certificate-controls" aria-label="Numerical certificate scenarios">@@CERTIFICATE_BUTTONS@@</div><div class="certificate-grid"><div><p class="case-status" id="case-status" data-certificate-status="REJECTED" role="status" aria-live="polite">Rejected</p><p id="case-explanation">The solver reports success, but the independently computed gap is too large. No state is committed.</p><p class="scope-note">For the stated convex objective and feasible domain, the linearization gap bounds objective suboptimality. Exact rational arithmetic on the finite binary inputs and outward rounding prevent a cancellation-created false certificate. The certificate does not establish prediction quality, source chronology or betting value.</p></div><dl><dt>Solver reported success</dt><dd id="solver-status">true</dd><dt>Feasibility violation</dt><dd id="primal-violation">0</dd><dt>Objective gap upper bound</dt><dd id="gap-bound">0.7</dd><dt>Numerical tolerance</dt><dd id="numerical-tolerance">1e-9</dd><dt>Predictive qualification</dt><dd>Not established</dd><dt>Fixture coordinates</dt><dd id="fixture-point">[0, 0, 0]</dd></dl></div><noscript><p>JavaScript is off. The rejected false-success example remains visible. Run the Python command below to reproduce every case.</p></noscript></div><div class="run-strip"><article class="run-step"><div class="eyebrow">Invented attempt 1</div><strong>2 new · 1 rejected</strong><p>Two states and receipts persist to a temporary local directory. The bad candidate leaves no accepted state.</p></article><article class="run-step"><div class="eyebrow">Invented recovery</div><strong>1 new · 2 reused</strong><p>Read back the exact saved bytes and independently recompute the certificate before reuse.</p></article><article class="run-step"><div class="eyebrow">Invented reentry</div><strong>0 new · 3 reused</strong><p>Completed work is not fitted or credited again. A stop between state and receipt publication has its own tested recovery path.</p></article></div><div class="callout"><strong>Run it without credentials.</strong><pre><code>python -m examples.fbs_contracts.certified_resume
python -m unittest examples.fbs_contracts.tests.test_certified_resume -v</code></pre><a href="../../examples/fbs_contracts/certified_resume.py">Inspect the implementation</a> · <a href="RECOVERY_AND_COVERAGE_2026-11-03.md">Read the mathematical and operational limits</a> · <a href="../../notebooks/fbs_branch_review.ipynb">Executed notebook</a></div></section>
<section id="season" class="section" aria-labelledby="season-title"><div class="section-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / Current-season evidence, with its actual meaning</div><h2 id="season-title">622 replayed games. Zero proven issued forecasts.</h2><p>The frozen recipe’s archived retrospective replay is preserved across all nine native weeks. It is separate from the blocked rolling-issue path and the 301-game monitor associated with the approximately 0.46 log-loss result.</p></div></div><div class="panel"><div class="tablewrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Original versus rolling evidence"><table><caption>2026 evidence classes remain separate</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Evidence</th><th scope="col">Games</th><th scope="col">Winner log loss</th><th scope="col">Margin MAE</th><th scope="col">Total MAE</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Frozen-recipe retrospective replay</th><td>622</td><td>0.513328</td><td>14.600</td><td>13.093</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Genuine rolling issued forecasts</th><td>0</td><td>Unavailable</td><td>Unavailable</td><td>Unavailable</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="week-controls"><label for="week-filter">Native week</label><select id="week-filter"><option value="all">All nine weeks</option><option value="1">Week 1</option><option value="2">Week 2</option><option value="3">Week 3</option><option value="4">Week 4</option><option value="5">Week 5</option><option value="6">Week 6</option><option value="7">Week 7</option><option value="8">Week 8</option><option value="9">Week 9</option></select><button id="weekly-csv" class="button small-button" type="button">Download weekly CSV</button></div><div class="tablewrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="All archived current-season native weeks"><table id="weekly-table"><caption>Preserved frozen-recipe replay, including losing predictions</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Native week</th><th scope="col">Games</th><th scope="col">Correct</th><th scope="col">Accuracy</th><th scope="col">Log loss</th><th scope="col">Brier</th><th scope="col">Margin MAE</th><th scope="col">Total MAE</th></tr></thead><tbody>@@WEEK_ROWS@@</tbody></table></div><p id="week-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="small">9 weeks · 622 games · retrospective replay</p></div><p class="scope-note">The separate 301-game monitor’s log loss is 0.465519. Different event populations prevent a direct 301-versus-622 improvement claim. Current outcomes cannot select or promote a model. Historical 2024/2025 winner, margin, total and calibration results remain in the <a href="index.html#explorer">complete seven-control explorer</a>.</p></section>
<section id="matched" class="section" aria-labelledby="matched-title"><div class="section-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">04 / Compare the same archived games</div><h2 id="matched-title">The matched DraftKings panels are stronger.</h2><p>Every row compares identical events and outcome labels. The original model’s values match the preserved 622-game replay. The smaller market-matched populations are shown explicitly.</p></div><span class="tag">Retrospective · no live execution claim</span></div><div class="panel"><div class="tablewrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Exact matched historical DraftKings comparisons"><table id="matched-table"><caption>Archived 2026 comparison; lower loss and RMSE are better</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Metric</th><th scope="col">Same games per side</th><th scope="col">Original replay</th><th scope="col">DraftKings archive</th></tr></thead><tbody>@@MATCHED_ROWS@@</tbody></table></div><p>Of 40 winner disagreements, the model alone was correct on 18 and DraftKings alone on 22. The model selected 132 of 192 winners correctly; DraftKings selected 136.</p><p class="scope-note">These aggregates were independently recomputed from preserved private rows, with exact event, label and model-value matching. Public cohort commitments make the published populations stable; the private predictions are not exposed. Actual pregame possession and execution at a stated cutoff are not established by this retrospective comparison. No significance, closing-line value or profitable strategy is inferred.</p><p class="scope-note"><strong>Kalshi and Polymarket:</strong> authenticated matched historical panels are unavailable. The absence of a panel does not prove the absence of a tradable product. Only these three providers belong to the active comparison scope.</p></div></section>
<section id="coverage" class="section" aria-labelledby="coverage-title"><div class="section-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / Make missingness visible</div><h2 id="coverage-title">A newer collector is not always newer FBS data.</h2><p>The V025 owner read an NFL-only latest collector and fell back to an older FBS seed. The preserved source snapshot was captured November 1 at 7:07 p.m. PST (November 2, 03:07 UTC); the owner assessment occurred November 3 at 1:38 p.m. PST (21:38 UTC). It is explicitly stale.</p></div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Eight event-time gaps, with concrete reasons</h3><div class="coverage-bar" aria-hidden="true"><div class="mapped"></div><div class="gap"></div></div><div class="legend"><span><strong>55 / 63</strong> event identity candidates</span><span><strong>6</strong> unresolved kickoff placeholders</span><span><strong>2</strong> explicit kickoff disagreements</span></div><p>All eight gaps retain their quarantine. The new source reader authenticates the newest known completed FBS catalogue before using it as a fallback. Exact game-ID schedule histories explain revisions; neither nickname tolerance nor a later observation is used to fabricate a contemporaneous quote.</p><p class="small">Observed inventory: 888 FBS-involving games · 622 completed · 500 completed FBS-versus-FBS · 63 scheduled in the stated seven-day window. These counts do not establish complete official or latest-source coverage.</p><div class="tablewrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Active provider evidence coverage"><table><caption>Active comparison scope: DraftKings, Kalshi and Polymarket. Event mappings are not executable price qualification.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Mapped / observed events</th><th scope="col">Mapped / observed game-market rows</th><th scope="col">Qualified current cutoff quotes</th><th scope="col">Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody>@@PROVIDER_ROWS@@</tbody></table></div><p class="small">Across the archived capture, 1,835 game-market rows comprise 1,603 mapped and 232 quarantined rows. Eighteen player-prop rows are counted separately. Polymarket US and global products require separate qualification. Legacy provider history is preserved, while new active comparisons use only these three providers.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>No actionable edge is asserted.</strong> There are zero qualified current cutoff quotes, zero genuine issued forecasts and no verified position/settlement ledger. Proposed stake is zero. Realized P&amp;L and ROI are unavailable, not fabricated zeros.</div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title"><div class="section-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">06 / Inspect and reproduce</div><h2 id="evidence-title">Public mechanisms. Explicit private boundaries.</h2></div></div><p><a href="V025_OPERATIONAL_REVIEW_2026-11-03.json">Full public aggregate export</a> · <a href="../../examples/fbs_contracts/tests/test_certified_resume.py">Adversarial checkpoint tests</a> · <a href="../../examples/review_lab/numerical_recovery.py">Shared exact certificate</a> · <a href="../../tracks/ncaaf/MODEL_CARD.md">FBS model card</a> · <a href="research.html">Completed V024 historical study</a></p><p>The public example performs small real computations on invented inputs. Audited private aggregates describe owner work; they do not enable public raw-data retraining. Private recipes, active weights, licensed observations, current forecasts and cloud identifiers remain outside this page. The repository has no blanket license covering all historical content.</p></section></main><footer class="shell footer"><p>Sports Edge Lab / NCAA FBS · Dated evidence, unchanged historical results, no promotion.</p></footer><script id="recovery-data" type="application/json">@@PAYLOAD@@</script><script src="recovery.js"></script></body></html>
